From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 22 Nov 2026 12:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] winedmo: Clear the WM reader shutdown flag when reopening.

reader_Close() sets demux_shutdown to stop the demux thread and leaves it
set. init_stream() only clears it after winedmo_demuxer_create(), but
wm_stream_read_cb() returns no data while it is set, so the demuxer probes
an empty stream: every Open/OpenStream on a reader that was closed before
fails with "Invalid data found when processing input".

Angel Wish (#982) reuses its WMA readers: it closes a reader and opens the
same IStream on it again. Its BGM stopped after the main menu and voices
never played. With the Windows version left at Windows 10, the first
failed reopen is followed by an assertion failure and the game stops
responding at the company logos.

Clear the flags before the demuxer is created. No demux thread runs here:
init_stream() is only called from Open/OpenStream, before the thread is
created, and reader_Close() has joined the previous one.
---
--- a/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
+++ b/dlls/winedmo/wm_reader.c
@@ -2261,6 +2261,13 @@
     reader->demuxer_stream.stream.p_read = wm_stream_read_cb;
     reader->demuxer_stream.position = 0;
 
+    /* reader_Close() leaves demux_shutdown set, and wm_stream_read_cb() returns
+     * no data while it is set. Clear it before the demuxer probes the stream,
+     * or reopening a closed reader fails with "Invalid data found". */
+    reader->demux_shutdown = false;
+    reader->read_flushing = false;
+    reader->read_seeking = false;
+
     if ((status = winedmo_demuxer_create(reader->filename, &reader->demuxer_stream.stream,
             reader->file_size, &reader->duration, &stream_count, NULL, &reader->demuxer)))
     {
